 links=[("Babur founds Mughal Empire","Akbar the Great","Babur's grandson Akbar turned a conquest into a lasting state, winning over Hindu Rajput princes through marriage alliances and tolerance."),
  ("Akbar the Great","Taj Mahal begun","Akbar's rich and stable empire reached its artistic peak under his grandson Shah Jahan, who built the Taj Mahal for his wife Mumtaz Mahal."),
  ("Taj Mahal begun","Aurangzeb dies → Mughal decline","Shah Jahan's son Aurangzeb imprisoned his father and spent decades on costly wars in the Deccan. His death in 1707 left an exhausted empire to quarrelling heirs."),
  ("Aurangzeb dies → Mughal decline","Nader Shah sacks Delhi","The weakened Mughal court could not stop the Persian ruler Nader Shah, who sacked Delhi and carried off the Peacock Throne."),
  ("Nader Shah sacks Delhi","Battle of Plassey","Mughal collapse left regional rulers, like the Nawab of Bengal, who could be defeated or bought by the East India Company.")],
